  urldate = {2025-04-11},
  abstract = {A semiempirical model of the infrared (IR) spectrum of the C60 molecule is proposed. The weak IR-active modes seen experimentally in a C60 crystalline sample are argued to be combination modes caused by anharmonicity. The origin of these two-mode excitations can be either mechanical (anharmonic interatomic forces) or electrical (nonlinear dipole-moment expansion in normal mode coordinates). It is shown that the electrical anharmonicity model exhibits basic features of the experimental spectrum while nonlinear dynamics would lead to a qualitatively different overall picture.},
