  abstract = {We have reexamined the infrared spectrum of ketene in the 3{$\mu$}m region, and analysed two B-type perpendicular bands; the stronger is associated with the fundamental {$\nu$}7 and the weaker with the combination band ( {$\nu$}2 + {$\nu$}8). Furthermore we have examined the millimeterwave spectrum up to 200 GHz and measured several pure rotational transitions. The ground state combination differences obtained from the infrared spectrum together with the microwave and the new millimeterwave transitions have been used to determine a complete set of ground state rotational and centrifugal distortion constants. The derived rotational constants are A = 282081 \textpm{} 12 MHzB = 10293.9722 \textpm{} 0.0059 MHzC = 9915.2396 \textpm{} 0.0062 MHz},
