  abstract = {Far-infrared and mid-infrared spectra of thioketene have been recorded over the region 200-1250 cm-1and transitions assigned from the {$\nu$}4, {$\nu$}5, {$\nu$}6, and {$\nu$}9fundamentals and {$\nu$}5+ {$\nu$}9\textleftarrow{} {$\nu$}9and {$\nu$}5+ {$\nu$}6\textleftarrow{} {$\nu$}6hot bands. Ground state combination differences from {$\nu$}4and {$\nu$}5, together with {$\nu$}6and {$\nu$}9transitions, lower state combination differences from the {$\nu$}5+ {$\nu$}9\textleftarrow{} {$\nu$}9and {$\nu$}5+ {$\nu$}6\textleftarrow{} {$\nu$}6hot bands, and previous millimeter-wave data, have been included in a combined fit of {$\nu$}6, {$\nu$}9, and the ground state. The stronga-axis Coriolis interaction between {$\nu$}6and {$\nu$}9has been treated along with thec-axis centrifugal distortion interaction between {$\nu$}9and the ground state. The magnitudes of these interactions are in agreement with values obtained fromab initiomolecular orbital calculations at the MP2/6-311G** and CCSD/6-311G** levels of theory.},
