  urldate = {2025-04-16},
  abstract = {The molecular structure of the C6H radical was studied by the ab-initio SCF method with the MIDI-4 basis set. Contrary to small even carbon-chains C2H and C4H, whose ground states arew 2{$\Sigma$}+, the electronic ground state of the C6H radical is likely to be 2{$\Pi$}, although the calculated energy difference between the 2{$\Pi$} state and 2{$\Sigma$}+ state is only 0.068 eV. The calculated rotational constant of the 2{$\Pi$} state is 1382 MHz and that of the 2{$\Sigma$}+ state is 1392 MHz. This calculation indicates that the C6H radical is responsible for the recently observed doublet peaks from TMC-1. The calculated dipole moment of the 2{$\Pi$} state is 5.0 debye and that of the 2{$\Sigma$}+ state is 1.0 debye.},
