  urldate = {2025-04-17},
  abstract = {The microwave spectrum of ethyl alcohol, C 2H 5OH, was investigated in the frequency region 8-34 Ge/sec. About thirteen lines were assigned to ground state transitions. The existence of the trans rotamer was verified. The rotational constants were determined as A = 34 891.68 Mc/sec, B = 9350.44 Mc/sec, C = 8135.23 Mc/sec for the ground vibrational state of the trans rotamer. From b-type transitions 2 11\textleftarrow 2 02, 3 12\textleftarrow 3 03, 4 13\textleftarrow 4 04, 3 03\textleftarrow 2 12 and 2 21\textleftarrow 3 12 the dipole moment {$\mu$} and its components {$\mu$}a and {$\mu$}b were evaluated as {$\mu$} = (1.441 \textpm{} 0.007) D, {$\mu$}a = (0.046 \textpm{} 0.014) D and {$\mu$}b = (1.438 \textpm{} 0.019) D, respectively. The results were critically examined in comparison with the data presented by the researchers, Imanov and Kadzhar, and Michielsen-Effinger.},
