  abstract = {We present searches for gas-phase CO\_2\_ features in the ISO-SWS infrared spectra of four deeply embedded massive young stars, which all show strong solid CO\_2\_ absorption. The abundance of gas-phase CO\_2\_ is at most 2x10\textasciicircum -7\textasciicircum{} with respect to H\_2\_, and is less than 5\% of that in the solid phase. This is in strong contrast to CO, which is a factor of 10-100 more abundant in the gas than in solid form in these objects. The gas/solid state ratios of CO\_2\_, CO and H\_2\_O are discussed in terms of the physical and chemical state of the clouds.},
